  UTestCase.Lexer - Lexer atom tests

  TTestCase suite for the token vocabulary (TPCVocabulary), the token stream
  (TPCTokenStream) and the lexer (TPCLexer). Fixtures are real files in
  tests\probe\lex; inputs a text editor cannot pin down (exact CR LF bytes,
  lone CR, line splices, multi-byte characters) are lexed from literal text
  via TokenizeBytes. Splice and newline tests compare Spelling exactly
  (research\cppmix\lexer-splice-tests.md, lexer-splice-trailing.md). The C++
  elements of a cppstart block (PREREQ-B, research\cppmix\sem\prereq-b\jump.md)
  are compared as 'tag:spelling@line:col' texts (DoElementsText). Integer
  literal bounds (F19) are rows in tests\probe\lex\ib (GENERATED by
  scripts\zb_cmpl\f19\gen_bounds.py), checked against the lexer (int_bounds)
  and the bundled clang on every supported target (int_bounds_witness). The
  float suffix tables (F63) likewise: float_suffixes (the lexer) and
  float_suffix_witness (the bundled clang, with the build's -std flag).

  Dependencies: StdApp.TestCase, StdApp.Base, StdApp.Utils, StdApp.Resources,
    PaskalCPP.Common, PaskalCPP.TokenStream, PaskalCPP.Lexer, PaskalCPP.ZigBuild
===============================================================================}

